Subject: [PATCH 05/35] dist: satisfy clippy under the all-features gate

The tree fails `clippy -D warnings --features all,dist-server` with the
current toolchain. The failing sites in this commit are in
src/bin/sccache-dist/build.rs (semicolon_if_nothing_returned,
collapsible_if, to_string_in_format_args, useless_borrows_in_formatting),
src/bin/sccache-dist/cmdline/mod.rs (large_enum_variant),
src/bin/sccache-dist/cmdline/parse.rs (implicit_clone,
semicolon_if_nothing_returned), src/bin/sccache-dist/main.rs
(collapsible_if) and src/dist/http.rs (collapsible_if,
semicolon_if_nothing_returned).

I applied the forms clippy suggests: trailing semicolons, collapsed
let-chains, dropped redundant borrows and to_string calls, a cloned String
instead of to_string on a dereference, and a boxed server Config in the
sccache-dist Command enum, with the one destructuring site in main.rs
adjusted to unbox it. Behaviour is unchanged.

