From d60ebd0dd395000b042040331527347d2b8732ff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Javier Tia <javier@peridio.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:07:20 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 13/35] dist/build: Test the production eviction path, not just
 Mutex::try_lock

The only eviction test locked and try-locked a Mutex it created itself,
so it passed whatever the eviction loop did. Deleting the re-prepared
check, skipping the lock prune, or taking a private lock instead of the
shared per-toolchain one all left every test green.

The loop becomes OverlayBuilder::evict_toolchains, called from
prepare_overlay_dirs with unchanged behavior, and an OverlayBuilder can
be built in a test without root because eviction never uses bubblewrap.
Three tests run the real method on temp directories: an idle victim is
deleted and its lock entry pruned, a victim whose prepare lock is held
