Subject: [PATCH 15/35] compiler: share the in-flight guard and the dist
 test-mock helpers

PreprocInflightGuard in c.rs and DistInflightGuard in compiler.rs were
two copies of the same RAII counter over different statics, so a fix to
one would not reach the other. They are now one InflightGuard over a
&'static AtomicUsize, with both statics and every log line unchanged.

The dist test mocks also repeated the same put_toolchain return and the
same "some data in <name>" Complete result in several clients. Two
helpers in test_dist replace those copies; per-mock behavior that
differs (submit_toolchain assertions and errors) is left alone.

Nothing asserted on the in-flight count, so removing the guard's
decrement left every test green. A unit test now checks that enter
counts and drop releases, and it fails when the decrement is removed.

