From b73aab490000ace2a99891b70329ca3bc352804d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Javier Tia <javier@peridio.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 17:32:28 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 16/35] dist/scheduler: treat a heartbeat without a report as
 no liveness information

A heartbeat from a server that predates the active-jobs report has no
list to compare against, and passing it through as an empty list makes
the scheduler read absence as "nothing is running". After two beats it
reclaims every Started job older than the grace, so a long compile on
such a server loses its slot while it still runs.

The scheduler entry point now takes Option<Vec<JobId>>. None still
registers and refreshes the server but skips the liveness lease and the
fixed backstop and leaves the stored last-reported set alone, so the
server is pruned only when it stops heartbeating. Some behaves as
before, pinned by a test that reclaims under an empty report. The one
production caller passes Some, and registration of a reportless server
logs once so the missing reclaim is visible.

Signed-off-by: Javier Tia <javier@peridio.com>
