From 65ea92a9baba228bfc9f705bcc4ba4ba83d192dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Javier Tia <javier@peridio.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 17:33:24 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 17/35] dist/http: accept heartbeats from servers that predate
 the active-jobs report

The heartbeat request gained a trailing active_jobs field, and bincode
is positional, so the new scheduler answers 400 to every stock or older
build server and the cluster silently loses its capacity after an
upgrade of the scheduler alone.

The route now buffers the body (capped at 1 MiB plus one byte) and
decodes it as the current layout, else as the five-field layout older
servers send, which reaches the scheduler as no active-jobs report. Both
attempts reject trailing bytes: the free bincode functions ignore them,
so a current body with junk appended, or one truncated inside its list,
could otherwise pass as the older layout and silently drop the job list.
The wire format servers send is unchanged. The trace line now logs the
job list instead of the whole request, which carried the signing key.

Signed-off-by: Javier Tia <javier@peridio.com>
---
