Subject: [PATCH 24/35] server: name the dropped output in the failure and log
 rejected uploads

The dropped-output arm printed the error with plain Display, which shows
only anyhow's outermost context ("failed to store `foo.o` to cache") and
hides the message that names the output the server did not return. The
test checked for "foo.o", which the outer context also contains, so it
could not tell the two apart.

The arm now prints the whole chain with `{:#}`, and the test checks the
root message names the output and appears in that chain. The upload
receiver also logs a rejected hash at warn, with the claimed id and the
computed digest, so an operator can tell a forged upload from a full
disk.

