Subject: [PATCH 25/35] dist: share the packable-file filter and drop dead
 deregister pool settings

add_dir_contents and add_shared_libraries each carried the same test for
which directory entries enter a toolchain package: a regular file, or a
symlink that resolves to one, with a dangling symlink skipped so one bad
link cannot abort the whole best-effort package. Two copies of that rule
can drift, and the next fix to it would have to find both.

Both now call one helper that keeps the dangling-link explanation. The
shutdown deregister client also set an idle connection pool it can never
use: it sends a single request and the process exits, so only the 2
second timeout matters and the pool settings are removed.

Signed-off-by: Javier Tia <javier@peridio.com>
