The fixes for older heartbeats, long compiles, forged and interrupted
uploads, a dropped output with fallback off and rlib trimming were each
unit tested, but the cluster-level behaviour (real scheduler, real build
server, real compiles) was only described, never run.

The script builds the worktree and a stock v0.19.0 sccache-dist, starts
them on 127.0.0.1 in a scratch directory and checks six scenarios,
printing a pass or fail line per check and a checks N/M count. Servers
run unprivileged through `unshare -Ur`, which satisfies the overlay
builder's root check without touching the host. The eviction-reuse and
deployment checks stay manual steps because they need multi-gigabyte
toolchains and the real hosts.

