From 8d794713e60bab04015542fb82cfe190bd950656 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Javier Tia <javier@peridio.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 11:52:10 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 28/35] Cargo.toml: require zstd 0.14

The zstd binding and its safe wrapper carry three RustSec findings
(context reuse across abandoned streams, an unchecked seekable offset,
and uninitialised memory after a failed legacy-frame streaming decode).
Their fixes exist only in zstd 0.14.3 and zstd-safe 8.2.0, so no
update inside the 0.13 series can clear them. The streaming-decoder
finding is reachable: the cache read path decodes entries through
copy_decode.

Only the requirement line and the two locked packages move. The code
calls copy_encode and copy_decode, whose signatures are unchanged, so
no source file changes and the stored frame format is the standard one.

Signed-off-by: Javier Tia <javier@peridio.com>
