Subject: [PATCH 29/35] Cargo.toml: require object 0.40

ruzstd, the zstd decoder behind the object-file parser, has a
decompression-bomb finding that is fixed only from ruzstd 0.9.1, and
object 0.37 pins the 0.8 series. Raising the requirement moves the
parser to a release that depends on the fixed decoder.

The code uses object only to read archive, Mach-O fat and ELF program
headers, and compiles unchanged at 0.40. The lock keeps an older
object release because the backtrace crate, enabled through anyhow's
backtrace feature, still requires the 0.37 series; that copy no longer
pulls the vulnerable decoder.

