From dd5e84aedfe12dedc43a5932f97904ee04d9eb4d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Javier Tia <javier@peridio.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 11:57:17 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 30/35] cache_io: port the cache entry writer to zip 9

Three RustSec findings against the zip 0.6 series (SUID bits and
symlinks preserved by the archive extraction calls) are fixed only from
zip 9.0.0. Nothing here calls extraction, but leaving an unmaintained
series in place means the scan stays red or a reasoned ignore must be
kept true by every future change.

The port is the file-options type, the call that builds it, and a
binding that no longer needs to be mutable because the writer's finish
now consumes it. Two tests pin the stored format first: a round trip of
an object, standard output, standard error and the file mode, and the
same assertions on a 325-byte entry produced by the pre-port code at
the base commit, so an entry written by the previous package is proven
readable by this one. The new zip pulls in nix and typed-path.

