From 0b53bb7cc5ad5e377de565e92fd9f8ef165cb1f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Javier Tia <javier@peridio.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 11:58:26 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 31/35] audit: accept the rsa timing finding that has no fix

After the dependency updates, the advisory scan reports one remaining
vulnerability: the Marvin timing side channel in rsa 0.9.10, for which
no fixed release exists. Left unrecorded it keeps the pre-push hook red
and forces every push to skip the hook, which hides the next finding
too.

The scan's project-level ignore file now lists only that identifier,
with the reason (rsa is compiled in only through the request-signing
crates of the object-storage layer, and this cluster's cache is local
disk, so no RSA private-key operation runs), the ceiling (valid only
while no cloud storage backend is configured with an RSA key) and the
upgrade trigger (a fixed rsa release, or a host configuring a cloud
backend). The hook command is unchanged. The file's directory is
gitignored, so it was added with a forced add.

Signed-off-by: Javier Tia <javier@peridio.com>
---
 .cargo/audit.toml | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 .cargo/audit.toml

diff --git a/.cargo/audit.toml b/.cargo/audit.toml
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..09ac6185
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.cargo/audit.toml
@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+[advisories]
+ignore = [
+    # RUSTSEC-2023-0071: rsa 0.9.10, Marvin Attack timing side channel.
+    # Reason: no fixed release exists. The crate is compiled in only through
+    # the request-signing crates (reqsign) of the object-storage layer, and
+    # this cluster's cache is local disk (`sccache --show-stats` prints
+    # "Cache location Local disk"), so no RSA private-key operation runs.
+    # Ceiling: valid only while no cloud storage backend is configured with an RSA key.
+    # Upgrade trigger: a fixed rsa release is published, or any host configures a cloud storage backend.
+    "RUSTSEC-2023-0071",
+]
-- 
Javier Tia


